# Deploy. Deploy is a module inside Toolbox, a view: it reads one Instance value and
# writes Game Data/, whose manifest is its hash. The manifest is an Instance input, so
# deploy state comes back the same way as everything else.
...@../styles
shape: sequence_diagram
instance: @../target-architecture.modbench_driven.instance
instance.label: Instance
tables: @../target-architecture.modbench_kernel.tables
tables.label: per-release tables
toolbox: @../target-architecture.modbench_driving.toolbox
toolbox.label: Toolbox
gamedata: @../target-architecture.modbench_data.gamedata
gamedata.label: Game Data/

instance -> toolbox: one value, with its sequence {class: loadout}
tables -> toolbox: load-order file destination {class: deploy}
toolbox -> toolbox: "deploy · purge, with the value" {class: deploy}
toolbox."deploy, inside Toolbox: hardlinks, manifest, first-deploy consent"
toolbox -> gamedata: hardlinks · manifest {class: deploy}
gamedata -> instance: "watch: the manifest" {class: signal}
instance -> toolbox: value, deploy state {class: loadout}
